      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "On desktop the feature request section links to a page with advice for submitting feature requests, the main one is that it should be one feature per post.\n\nFor VRChats end, they can tie a post from here into thier development pipeline.\n\nFor users, what tends to happen is that when two or more things are posted, one of them will dominate discussion.\n\nAs a PCVR user, I hope that the additional ram in the Quest 3 is enough to reduce complaints of crashing compared to q2. It is only 2gb..\n\nAs for the additional processing power, VRChat worlds are user generated, so I expect the computing power to be readily eaten up by world authors",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-10-05T08:47:18.301Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "add support for the new quest 3 upper body tracking (eg elbows arms hips and waist)  and the improved power like bigger worlds or shaders or better lighting, and add quest 3 controller models instead of the quest 1 models being shown",
